{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/197332-conspiracy-pisces-the-section","id":197332,"title":"Conspiracy: PISCES, \"The Section\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-14T19:42:48-07:00","id":197332,"title":"Conspiracy: PISCES, \"The Section\"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">More <i>Delta Green</i> material converted to Hunter! These guys are the UK's official answer to supernatural problems; a bunch of spies and psychics who happen to have a nasty issue with alien brain bugs who worship Azathoth. I don't quite have all this written up (the Insects from Shaggai deserve a write-up) and their Endowment really would just be the already printed Supernatural Merits in GMC, but here's what I've got. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> Within the United Kingdom and its former colonial holdings, the servants of unholy powers find themselves pursued by an implacable foe. PISCES - the Paranormal Intelligence Section for Counter-Intelligence, Espionage, and Sabotage - has been upholding a state-sponsored Vigil since the gruesome years of the Great War, and keeps up their hunt to this day. They have a cadre of psychics and the full backing of the government at their disposal, and a dark secret that many have died to keep.<br /> <br /> PISCES began as a miserable failure of a secret Royal Navy program in the closing days of the 1800s century, designed to utilize self-described mystics, seers, and clairvoyants as wartime intelligence assets. The project had all but nonexistent results, but was nonetheless reactivated in a fit of desperation in 1916. The psychic \u2018Talents\u2019 of what was then known as MI-13, the \u201cSpecial Reconnaissance Section,\u201d met with fair success, but was disregarded by a number of skeptics and swiftly defunded in the days after the war\u2019s close.<br /> <br /> MI-13 had its second chance in 1940, when a former Talent predicted the German offensive into Belgium. Churchill took notice of the precognitive warning once it came true and quickly threw support into the newly-christened PISCES, who put their newfound sway to quick use in opposing Nazi and Imperial Japanese efforts to weaponize the supernatural. Post-WW2, \u201cthe Section\u201d busied itself with cleaning up a myriad number of cults throughout Her Majesty\u2019s territories and keeping close tabs on some thoroughly unpleasant Soviet projects.<br /> <br /> Today, PISCES is a black budget intelligence agency that operates entirely off the books; they answer exclusively to the Prime Minister, and are largely given free rein to do what they must. Few outside the Section know of its existence, and many of the lower-ranking agents believe they simply work for an obscure portion of MI-6. They still pursue their earliest purpose - the study and quantification of psychic abilities, and the recruitment of potential Talents - with equal fervor to their hunt for servants of unseemly powers within the United Kingdom.<br /> <br /> <b>The Dirty Secret</b><br /> PISCES is hopelessly compromised by the enemy. It\u2019s not the Communists who freely infested the British intelligence community during the Cold War (though that whole fiasco ended may careers and effectively shattered credibility for decades), but something far worse than any human malice. They resemble insects - large, ugly, winged things - that claim to come from a far-off world, and worship a dreadful god that predates humanity. These insects have infested the Section ever since an otherwise-successful raid on a dreadful Welsh village full of human cultists (some of which who still rot in secret prison cells) in the late 1960s.<br /> <br /> The good news is, these creatures are horrendous bigots. They loathe the existence of other supernatural beings and hope to destroy any religion other than their own. The Insects are strange parasites, capable of becoming immaterial and melding with the ill-understood quantum fabric of the human mind; from there, they exist in an unnatural symbiosis that grants the host body alien knowledge but tragically annihilates one\u2019s mental health in a matter of years. PISCES\u2019 membership is roughly 10% infested by the Insects, but it\u2019s the 10% that handles the Section\u2019s management and the training of new agents, in addition to their internal police. It\u2019s easy for the Insects to purge those who learn of the truth by simply claiming that they had attempted to betray the nation.<br /> <br /> As such, PISCES is a legitimate (if secret) intelligence agency that ruthlessly hunts down servants of the monsters that rule the night; it just happens to be one driven by one group of horrors whose primary motivation is alien religious zeal. Is it a matter of accepting a lesser evil in the name of the greater good? The question doesn\u2019t much matter, for no one will ever know\u2026 or so PISCES hopes.<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> PISCES got its start hunting down entirely mortal threats, and they continue to do so to this day, albeit in a lesser capacity; threats to national security are usually discovered in the course of other investigations, and are usually passed on to \u2018lesser\u2019 agencies. The Section has bigger fish to fry.<br /> Sorcerers draw the brunt of their attention. Remnants of their wartime foes still act today, and the combined generational duty mingles with the disgust of the Insects (for their false gods and for their hubris to pursue magic that should solely belong to them and their few thralls) to create real blinders on any other threat. Occult texts are collected at any available opportunity and thrown into an archive in London, while cultists end up languishing indefinitely in black site prisons where they can be interrogated for what they know.<br /> <br /> Other monsters are handled by PISCES as well, though with less rancor. Anything involving vampires, shapechangers, and anything else that defies reason (one well-hidden case involved a mummy breaking free from study in London and destroying a good three city blocks) comes across the desks of the Section and is dealt with in a timely manner. Infested with aliens or not, PISCES prides itself on efficiency.<br /> <br /> PISCES has a large collection of occult texts in their archive in London, and a top-secret site off the Scottish coast holds a number of more dangerous artifacts along with many madmen whose secrets make them too valuable to kill; between these two resources, the Section is surprisingly well-informed about most any supernatural threat. The Insects give their information to their hosts that exceeds anything most humans might know, but few of the infected agents see work in the field.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You were a rising star in MI-6, fueled by a genuine desire to keep your country safe. That meteoric climb was halted when you came across something you couldn\u2019t explain; they transferred you to PISCES within the week, and you\u2019ve taken to it swimmingly.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You\u2019ve always been able to see and hear things nobody else could, but hid it in order to avoid being branded a lunatic. Somehow, the Section found you and gave you an offer; you accepted, not out of any desire to do the work, but because it pays better than any alternative.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You have one of the Insects in your brain, though you don\u2019t remember that most days. Its consciousness feels like your own, and the knowledge it gives you feels like uncanny insight you didn\u2019t know you had. All that matters to you is keeping the Section internally secure.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You were a witch who got sloppy; PISCES kicked down your door and locked you away in one of their prisons. Their offer was simple; use what you know to protect the UK, or have your body dumped into the sea. You took the deal happily enough, but are starting to think something fishy is going on.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-14-2014, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T20:12:19-07:00","id":197349,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm considering; specific mention of the Mythos was purged from my Delta Green writeup, yet I ran with the Insects from Shaggai for these guys. Would it be better to just have their dirty secret be that the directors of the Section are simply tainted by worship of something inhuman (and ill-defined) that drives them to the same extremes that the Insects do in DG canon. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T20:24:45-07:00","id":197372,"title":"","content":"Probably human worshipers. I like the Shan, but they really don't quite have a place when actual, mystically based demonic possession happens on Earth, with the native spiritual ecology. The human host comes out better for it, too! ...Relatively.<br /> <br /> Maybe they found an artifact which helped them with engineering their Endowment...and it turned out to be intelligent, having a lot of the Xada Hglan Shan's motives of eradicating all &quot;false beliefs&quot;, defined as &quot;anything vaguely religious or spiritual not based in what the artifact thinks it knows.&quot; I'd leave the ultimate motives for that ambiguous-maybe it's just a religious zealot, but it could also be that it thinks it's minimizing the chance for religious conflict and self-destruction through mysticism.<br /> <br /> Also leaves open the possibility that a few things might pass its inspection, and thus it gets PISCES to <i>protect </i>those religious beliefs and sorcerers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T02:35:38-07:00","id":197724,"title":"","content":"I find that radically changes what they are; they're body-swapping monsters controlling people not evil cultists themselves. As a conspiracy/compact in general play that's not really a problem but in stories actually dealing with PISCES that removes a lot of the scariness and paranoia of them; that the shan can jump hosts, even to people who they are fighting; and you really don't have any way to tell until you take a surgical drill to their head.<br /> <br /> Also, the opportunity to have their endowment be a shan host is kinda awesome to my mind.<br /> <br /> Also also, why the change from MI5 to MI6?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T11:13:04-07:00","id":198067,"title":"","content":"Problem with the Insects from Shaggai is the sheer power of deprotagonisation; as far as I know, there's no way to get them out beyond brain surgery, and they can and eventually will drive hosts insane. Good if you want doomed characters or antagonists, crap for any other story<br /> <br /> With a Hunter group, I at least should expect to be able to play them without necessitating a &quot;turning against the Conspiracy&quot; plotline at some point if the players with to remain slightly independent. Cherion, the Knight's of Saint George, the Shulpites; all are extremely amoral, but they have human and often understandable motives, sometimes even admirable ones.<br /> <br /> The Shan want to conquer Earth, plain and simple. The fact that the sane(r) portion of the race wants to do it for religious reasons is an interesting spin on things, but ultimately just because it invokes different imagery, more of an alien bunch of Crusaders and holy knights who sing strange hymns while slicing people apart, temples torn down and well-kept shrines built from the rubble-that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Here's a thought though; why not make the relationship more symbiotic? The Shan, upon insinuating themselves into PISCES, made an offer; they assist in hunting down sorcerers and religious extremists, the humans help them in gradual eradication of the &quot;false, self-destructive religions&quot; that scar the planet. Thing is, if you ask a Shan about this, they will happily explain that they think they're helping; to them, they see this stupid, stupid idea of religion and science being mutual foes, and with that <i>lovely </i>disconnect, we get things like the anti-vaccination movement, prejudice against intellectuals, and the idea that some things should not be known (ridiculous, they say-they looked straight into the body of the Nuclear Chaos and all that happened to them - that they noticed - was the ability to phase through walls and possess people!). So really, they're just trying to assist the natives of this planet, educate them. With guns, if needed.<br /> <br /> Sort of like Europeans spreading their proper, nonpagan culture, the analogy they do <i>not </i>get, let alone use.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, this isn't entirely altruistic-the Shan want to get back to their empire, or at least it's ruins, and they've figured out it's probably easier to get humans as allies rather than collateral damage in this. Humans could serve as a useful client race to help it become something even stronger than it was before. To do that requires humans survive to that point, and besides, if the world becomes a nuclear, barren wasteland it's not exactly possible for them to fix their ship given the lack of materials. This could be the motive for eradication of the supernatural, they want humans to be <i>predictable, </i>none of that &quot;may shapeshift into giant wolf in a few cases&quot; business and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-15-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T00:33:50-07:00","id":198642,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty interesting take. You don't need the insanity thing, that's really just because it's a CoC monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shan want to conquer Earth, plain and simple. </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Elders of the Shan want to leave. Stamping out other 'religions' is just general principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}